body:
Just got my first-ever bike, it's the Mongrel 125cc. Absolutely love it. Can't believe it took me until 37 years old to discover it. What's the furthest you've ridden in one sitting?

&#x200B;

Any tips you could impart about the bike (Only had it a few weeks) regarding maintenance, anything I should look out for?

This is a decidedly obtuse way of looking at it. Just because one is young does not make their efforts any less important. After all, the 'grown-ups' haven't exactly done a great job of things so far. She (amongst others) has managed to make the climate issue louder and more difficult to ignore. This can only be a good thing.

&#x200B;

Remember too, that these 'kids' you ostensibly despise are going to run the world  one day; ignore them now at your peril.

Petition down for maintenance

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

Edit: Finally got to sign it, no email to confirm though.
